<h2>What changes between Growth, Pro and Enterprise?</h2><p>Growth covers the basic ticket queue and self-service setup. Pro is the tier to review when you need custom dashboards, intelligent routing or several SLA policies. Enterprise adds more controls for skill-based routing, sandbox use and audit visibility. These differences matter when your team has several queues or compliance needs: the feature list on a vendor site can include items that are not part of the plan you are considering. Map each must-have feature to the exact plan before calculating cost.</p><h2>How to tell if the workflow is improving</h2><p>Measure a small baseline before changing the process. Track incoming ticket volume, unassigned work, first response, resolution time and the questions that repeat most often. A useful knowledge base should reduce avoidable contacts without making it harder for customers to reach a person. Review the numbers after agents have used the setup for a few weeks, and adjust ticket categories or saved replies only when the data shows a clear problem.</p>
